Start native ALSA movie playback with source PCM and observe real pending frames.

SDL 2.32 writes silence while a newly opened device is paused. Actual native
SDL/ALSA INTRO.AVI output contained three extra 1024-frame silent periods
before otherwise exact source PCM. Queue-empty also reports backend delivery,
not device consumption. Wine 10's S16 WaveOut ALSA path starts by writing source
data, with 10-ms hardware periods and four periods of buffering.

Use that ALSA device profile when the native SDL audio driver is ALSA. Preserve
SDL rendering, input and the other SDL audio drivers. Fill the initial device
buffer from source sample zero before starting the producer thread. Later
silence remains actual device output until the MCI close; no reference PCM,
fixed tail padding, data shifting or output fitting is used. Check ALSA delay
for completion and reject an unrecoverable output error as MCI failure.

An actual full intro device observation removes the startup mismatch for all
6039616 source bytes in accepted and played PCM. Whole lifetime silence tails
and common original/port A/V clocks remain unverified; this is not full parity.

